            "review_title": "Review at Kinh Do Hanoi Cafe 252 Hang Bong",
            "review_text": "Lua\nHanoi, Vietnam21 contributions\n1\nWonderful Vietnamese/French bakery and cafe\nJun 2018 • Family\nWe have been coming here for over 20 years and it is one of our favorites in Hanoi! The 252 is run by the granddaughter of the original owner, who started this place during the war. It was one of the first places in Vietnam that had French foods, and they still use the recipes from that time. They were even invited back by Ho Chi Minh himself after they they left the country to escape the violence! The 252 is well known for their delicious homemade yogurt (the best in Hanoi, in my opinion), which is not sweet (just how we like it!), pasteries, flan, fresh fruit smoothies and cháo (rice porridge), although they have nearly 100 available foods to try. The owner is a wonderful woman who loves her customers, works hard to keep the cafe running, pays her workers fairly, and always welcomes us with a smile and open arms. She can usually be found in the corner doing calculations. We adore her!\nRead more\nWritten June 23, 2018",
            "rating": 3.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
