            "review_title": "Review at Kinh Do Hanoi Cafe 252 Hang Bong",
            "review_text": "Tran L\nEdinburgh, United Kingdom34 contributions\n0\nGreat old cafe recommended for travelers and locals\nJan 2018 • Family\nI have been to this cafe since I was little. They served new baked everyday even though they do not have a lot of variety. The food and drink flavor are completely different from everywhere else which reminds me of the old Hanoi because they are homemade I guess. For example their pizza is not covered in layers of cheese but taste amazing. My favorite is their lemon tart with a perfect blend of sourness and sweetness. I think they only have less customers than before due to lots of new bakery chains but their quality is still unbeatable. If you do not like eating their, just take away. I hope they will refurbish the interior so the cafe will be more welcoming by the public.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 2, 2018",
            "rating": 4.0,
